<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42656" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sarra</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sara</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 2,
			6, 58</span></i>), ae, f., Heb. Zor. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The city of Tyre</i>, <i>in
				Phœnicia</i>, <i>celebrated for its
				purple dye</i>: Poenos Sarrā oriundos, Enn. ap. Prob.
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				G. 2, 506</span></i>; cf. Serv. ad loc., and <i><span class="en">Gell. 14,
				6, 4</span></i>: purpuram ex Sarā tibi Attuli, Plaut. l.
			l.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sarrānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Sarra</i>, i. e., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Tyrian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil. 1,
					72</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Leptis,</span>”
				<i>built by the Tyrians</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					256</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 506</span></i>
			; Col. poët. 10, 287; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					15, 205</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aulaea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					10, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">violae,</span>”
				<i>purple-red</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					9, 4, 4</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>Carthaginian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Juno (especially honored in Carthage),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					6, 468</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9,
					319</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">navita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7,
					432</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">numina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					46</span></i>
			.</div>
